3. *Important Preparation Instructions*
•	Keep your prototype ready for demonstration, if available.
•	If you do not have a physical or working prototype, keep a clear diagram, design, or visual representation of your solution ready.
•	All team members should understand the idea and their respective contributions.
•	Keep your pitch crisp, clear, and within the 3-minute time limit.
•	Be prepared to answer questions confidently. Understand your idea rather than memorising answers.
•	Support your responses with research, examples, and actual progress wherever possible.
•	Join the Google Meet a 5 minutes before your allotted slot. The system name should be your UID or Idea Name
•	Ensure you have a stable internet connection, a working microphone, and a quiet environment.

Remember: The jury is interested not just in your idea, but also in how well you understand the problem, your approach to solving it, and your ability to turn it into reality. Be honest about what you have achieved and what is still in progress.

